kosha thermal-conductivity

  -- rate at which heat flows through a material. k in W/(m·K).
  -- conductors: metals (free electrons carry heat). Ag:429, Cu:401, Al:237, Fe:80.
  -- insulators: wood:0.13, rubber:0.16, air:0.025, glass:1.0.
  -- why metal feels cold and wood feels warm at same temperature:
  --   metal draws heat from hand fast. wood draws slowly. sensation is rate, not temperature.

